---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { MethodologyAccordion } from "../../components/AnalysisPageSections";
---

<Layout
  role="visitor"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: "Home", href: "/" },
    { label: "Methods", href: "/methods/evaluation-framework" },
    { label: "Data quality & curation" },
  ]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8 py-12 max-w-4xl">
    <div class="mb-10">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-dark mb-3">
        Data Quality & Curation
      </h1>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-lg">
        How data submitted by Living Labs is validated, curated, and prepared
        for display in the SUM Open Data Platform.
      </p>
    </div>

    <MethodologyAccordion
      title="Validation workflow"
      subtitle="Steps from submission to publication"
      content=""
      defaultOpen={true}
    >
      <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Submitted KPI data passes through the following validation stages
          before appearing in public dashboards:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 ml-4">
          <li>
            <strong>Format check</strong> — Values must be numerical and within
            plausible ranges for each KPI definition. Records with missing
            required fields are flagged for review.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Temporal consistency</strong> — Before and after dates are
            checked for logical ordering. Results submitted without a
            corresponding baseline are noted as incomplete.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cross-lab comparison</strong> — Outlier detection flags
            values that deviate significantly from the distribution across all
            Living Labs, triggering manual review.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Curator review</strong> — A designated data curator reviews
            flagged records and either approves, requests correction, or
            excludes them from analysis.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Publication</strong> — Approved data is published to the
            platform and becomes available in KPI dashboards, impact analysis,
            and MCDA tools.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </MethodologyAccordion>

    <MethodologyAccordion
      title="Curator role"
      subtitle="Who is responsible for data quality"
      content=""
    >
      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <div
          class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-200 rounded-lg p-4 text-yellow-800"
        >
          <strong>Placeholder</strong> — The designated curator role is to be
          confirmed by the SUM consortium. This section will be updated once the
          responsible party and contact details are confirmed.
        </div>
        <p>
          The data curator is responsible for reviewing flagged submissions,
          maintaining consistency across Living Lab data, and coordinating with
          lab administrators to resolve data quality issues.
        </p>
      </div>
    </MethodologyAccordion>

    <MethodologyAccordion
      title="Review cadence"
      subtitle="How often data is reviewed and updated"
      content=""
    >
      <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <div
          class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-200 rounded-lg p-4 text-yellow-800"
        >
          <strong>Placeholder</strong> — The review cadence (quarterly / on
          data submission / on request) is to be confirmed by the consortium.
        </div>
        <p>
          Once confirmed, this section will describe the schedule for periodic
          data review, including how Living Labs are notified of review windows
          and how corrections are incorporated.
        </p>
      </div>
    </MethodologyAccordion>

    <MethodologyAccordion
      title="Display rules"
      subtitle="How incomplete or invalid data is handled in dashboards"
      content=""
    >
      <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          The platform applies the following rules when displaying data in
          dashboards and analysis tools:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 ml-4">
          <li>
            <strong>Missing KPI values</strong> — Labs without data for a given
            KPI are excluded from that KPI's charts. The chart caption notes the
            number of labs with available data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Incomplete before/after pairs</strong> — Impact analysis
            requires both baseline and post-intervention data. Labs with only
            one measurement are excluded from regression calculations but may
            appear in trend charts.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Empty measure records</strong> — Labs with no policy
            measures recorded are excluded from MCDA and impact analysis to
            avoid skewing results.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Invalid coordinates</strong> — Labs without valid geographic
            coordinates are excluded from the map view.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </MethodologyAccordion>
  </div>
</Layout>
